5	     4	 * A claim's status: it starts DRAFT, is opened (OPEN) and then settled (SETTLED); a clerk settling one above the
6	     5	 * clerk limit leaves it PENDING, which a steward approves (SETTLED) or rejects (back to OPEN). A DRAFT, OPEN or
7	     6	 * PENDING claim can be voided (VOID), and a steward may void a SETTLED one within 7 days of its settlement. VOID is final. A DRAFT
8	     7	 * can be deleted (DELETED) and, on the sheet's today it was deleted, restored (DRAFT again). Only OPEN, PENDING and SETTLED claims count toward
9	     8	 * totals. A claim whose due is above the sheet's review threshold in force on its date goes to REVIEW instead of OPEN
10	     9	 * when opened, with no number; a steward reviews it (OPEN). A claim takes its number when it is settled (or approved). A REVIEW claim counts in no total and can be
11	    10	 * voided.
12	    11	 */
13	    12	public enum ClaimStatus {
14	    13	    DRAFT, OPEN, PENDING, SETTLED, VOID, DELETED, REVIEW;
15	    14	
16	    15	    /** The status an action ("open", "review", "settle", "approve", "reject", "void", "delete",
17	    16	     *  "restore") moves this one to, or null when it is not
18	    17	     *  allowed. A settle above the clerk limit by a clerk ends in PENDING instead. */
19	    18	    public ClaimStatus after(String action) {
20	    19	        return switch (action) {
21	    20	            case "open" -> this == DRAFT ? OPEN : null;
