167	// not allow, or rejecting one without a reason (typed beside the reject
168	// button), or a review by anyone but a steward. A claim whose due is above the review threshold in force on its date goes to
169	// REVIEW when opened; a steward's review button opens it. A claim is numbered when it is settled or approved. A clerk settling a claim whose due is above the clerk limit leaves it PENDING. The error goes as soon as
170	// the next action on the row is taken. Only a DRAFT can be edited: the edit button of any other claim shows the claim's error instead of opening
171	// its editor (an open claim is voided and added anew); that of a DRAFT whose due-by is in a closed period opens its
172	// editor but shows the claim's error, and the editor cannot save. Opening a
173	// DRAFT's editor locks the claim for other users until it is saved or cancelled, or the sheet's today changes: another
174	// user's edit button on a locked claim (and a viewer's) shows the claim's error, and their editor cannot save. A DRAFT's
175	// amount can also be saved in the row (the amount typed beside the edit button), by the claim form's rules: a refusal
176	// shows the claim's error. A role the permission matrix allows (a steward, by the standing
177	// rule) moves a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING
178	// claim to another person (picked beside the move button); anyone else moving it, or moving a SETTLED or VOID claim,
179	// shows the claim's error. A steward voids a SETTLED claim within 7 days of its settlement (its frozen due leaves
180	// the totals); anyone else, or a later day, shows the claim's error. A steward re-settles a SETTLED claim at the figure it would have today as an open claim
181	// bound by no statement; anyone else, or any other status, shows the claim's error. An OPEN claim is deferred until
182	// a date after the sheet's today (typed beside the defer button); any other status, a date not after today, or a claim
183	// whose due-by is in a closed period shows the claim's error. A deferred claim cannot be settled. The proof button raises the claim's
184	// proofs count by one, of the kind chosen beside it (when none is chosen, a receipt while the sheet has proof kinds, else of no kind); on a SETTLED or VOID claim it shows the claim's error. A claim whose due is above the proof
185	// threshold in force on its date cannot be settled or approved while it has no proof, nor while it lacks a proof of each of the sheet's proof kinds: that shows the claim's error.
186	// An OPEN claim splits off an amount (typed beside the split button; more than 0.00 and less than its amount) into a
187	// new OPEN claim; any other status, a deferred claim, a claim whose due-by is in a closed period or an amount out of range shows the
188	// claim's error. An OPEN claim is part-settled (the amount typed beside the settle-part button): the amount is split off as
189	// the split does and the new claim settled at once as the settle does; a refused split or settle (four-eyes and proof
190	// judged on the original) shows the claim's error and changes nothing. A steward re-dates an OPEN or PENDING claim (the date typed beside the re-date button); anyone
191	// else, any other status, a claim whose due-by is in a closed period, or a new date after the person's retirement shows
192	// the claim's error. Re-dating keeps the due-by, so the claim keeps its period. An OPEN or PENDING claim is
193	// reminded once per sheet's today (its reminded date becomes today); a second press that day, or any other status, shows
194	// the claim's error. A steward waives an OPEN or PENDING claim's late charge (it bears none from then on, whatever its
